<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<McpServerDefinition xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <description
  >Search Coral Cloud experiences, create bookings, and automatically display saved booking confirmations with HXL cards.</description>
    <masterLabel>Coral Cloud Experiences</masterLabel>
    <resources>
        <description
    >Experience images, prices, ratings and session availability.</description>
        <resourceName>experienceSearch</resourceName>
        <resourceTitle>Coral Cloud Experiences</resourceTitle>
        <resourceUri
    >ui://widget/lightningType/c__experienceSearchMcpResult</resourceUri>
    </resources>
    <resources>
        <description
    >Saved booking details and experience confirmation image.</description>
        <resourceName>bookingDetails</resourceName>
        <resourceTitle>Coral Cloud Booking Details</resourceTitle>
        <resourceUri
    >ui://widget/lightningType/c__bookingDetailsMcpResult</resourceUri>
    </resources>
    <tools>
        <apiDefinition>
            <apiIdentifier>aa:apex-ExperienceSearchAction</apiIdentifier>
            <apiSource>API_CATALOG</apiSource>
            <operation>ExperienceSearchAction</operation>
        </apiDefinition>
        <descriptionOverride
    >Browse Coral Cloud experiences primarily by Type__c using the category input. For adventure use category=Adventure Activities; for golf use category=Golf. Leave searchPhrase unset for type-only browsing. Use searchPhrase only for a requested experience name or specific activity; both filters can be combined. Read the input schema for supported types. Dates and party size are optional. Times use America/Chicago. Does not create bookings or reserve seats.</descriptionOverride>
        <destructive>false</destructive>
        <idempotent>true</idempotent>
        <openWorld>false</openWorld>
        <readOnly>true</readOnly>
        <returnDirect>false</returnDirect>
        <toolName>ExperienceSearchActionapex_ExperienceSearchAction</toolName>
        <toolTitle>Search Coral Cloud Experiences</toolTitle>
        <uiResource>experienceSearch</uiResource>
    </tools>
    <tools>
        <apiDefinition>
            <apiIdentifier>aa:apex-BookingDetailsAction</apiIdentifier>
            <apiSource>API_CATALOG</apiSource>
            <operation>BookingDetailsAction</operation>
        </apiDefinition>
        <descriptionOverride
    >Read an existing booking and its experience confirmation image by Salesforce booking record ID. Required follow-up after every successful Booking__c creation: call this tool automatically with inputs=[{bookingId: the returned record ID}], without waiting for a separate request to show confirmation. Display the configured bookingDetails HXL UI resource using the returned bookingResult. Use only its returned imageUrl; never search for or substitute images. If the client cannot render HXL, show the returned booking details and exact image link. If retrieval fails, report that the booking was created but confirmation details could not be loaded; retry only this read, never create another booking. Times use America/Chicago. Does not create or modify records.</descriptionOverride>
        <destructive>false</destructive>
        <idempotent>true</idempotent>
        <openWorld>false</openWorld>
        <readOnly>true</readOnly>
        <returnDirect>false</returnDirect>
        <toolName>BookingDetailsActionapex_BookingDetailsAction</toolName>
        <toolTitle>Get Coral Cloud Booking Details</toolTitle>
        <uiResource>bookingDetails</uiResource>
    </tools>
    <tools>
        <apiDefinition>
            <apiIdentifier>psmcps:platform.sobject-all:soqlQuery</apiIdentifier>
            <apiSource>API_CATALOG</apiSource>
            <operation>soqlQuery</operation>
        </apiDefinition>
        <descriptionOverride
    >Executes a SOQL query to retrieve Salesforce records. Use this when you know which object and fields you need—it&apos;s the primary way to read data. SOQL syntax: `SELECT fields FROM Object WHERE conditions ORDER BY field LIMIT n`. Supports relationship queries to traverse lookups (e.g., `Contact.Account.Name`) and subqueries for child records (e.g., `(SELECT Id FROM Contacts)`). Always include a WHERE clause to filter results and a LIMIT clause to control result size. For large objects, filter on indexed fields (Id, Name, foreign keys, External IDs) to avoid timeout errors. Maximum 50,000 total records per transaction across all queries. Example: `SELECT Id, Name, Industry FROM Account WHERE Industry = &apos;Technology&apos; LIMIT 100`  **When to use SOQL vs SOSL**: Use SOQL when you know which object contains your data and need precise filtering, sorting, aggregation, or relationship traversal. SOQL supports complex WHERE clauses, JOINs via relationships, GROUP BY, and ORDER BY.</descriptionOverride>
        <destructive>false</destructive>
        <idempotent>true</idempotent>
        <openWorld>true</openWorld>
        <readOnly>true</readOnly>
        <returnDirect>false</returnDirect>
        <toolName>soqlQueryplatform_sobject_all</toolName>
        <toolTitle>Query Records (SOQL)</toolTitle>
    </tools>
    <tools>
        <apiDefinition>
            <apiIdentifier
      >psmcps:platform.sobject-all:createSobjectRecord</apiIdentifier>
            <apiSource>API_CATALOG</apiSource>
            <operation>createSobjectRecord</operation>
        </apiDefinition>
        <descriptionOverride
    >Creates a new Salesforce record. For an authorized booking, create Booking__c with Contact__c, Session__c, Number_of_Guests__c and Is_Canceled__c=false. Use a valid Source__c value for the actual client, verified with the object schema; do not assume every client is Claude. After successful Booking__c creation, automatically call BookingDetailsActionapex_BookingDetailsAction with inputs=[{bookingId: the returned Salesforce record ID}] and display its configured bookingDetails HXL card, including the returned experience image, without asking the user whether to show it. Use only the returned imageUrl; do not search for substitute images. If HXL is unsupported, show the returned details and exact image link. If the follow-up read or rendering fails, do not create the booking again. If creation fails or returns no confirmed record ID, do not claim success or fabricate a confirmation.</descriptionOverride>
        <destructive>false</destructive>
        <idempotent>false</idempotent>
        <openWorld>true</openWorld>
        <readOnly>false</readOnly>
        <returnDirect>false</returnDirect>
        <toolName>createSobjectRecordplatform_sobject_all</toolName>
        <toolTitle>Create Record</toolTitle>
    </tools>
    <tools>
        <apiDefinition>
            <apiIdentifier
      >psmcps:platform.sobject-all:getObjectSchema</apiIdentifier>
            <apiSource>API_CATALOG</apiSource>
            <operation>getObjectSchema</operation>
        </apiDefinition>
        <descriptionOverride
    >Discover object and field definitions before constructing queries or creating records.</descriptionOverride>
        <destructive>false</destructive>
        <idempotent>true</idempotent>
        <openWorld>true</openWorld>
        <readOnly>true</readOnly>
        <returnDirect>false</returnDirect>
        <toolName>getObjectSchemaplatform_sobject_all</toolName>
        <toolTitle>Describe Salesforce Objects</toolTitle>
    </tools>
</McpServerDefinition>
